WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.909
At an agency our size, the
limits bite in predictable ways,

2
00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:07.275
and this is the program's
design guidance for each.

3
00:00:07.275 --> 00:00:10.625
A workflow per organization
runs out of a hundred fast,

4
00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:13.900
so build a few general
workflows that branch on codes.

5
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.188
Build one reusable Logic
App per integration.

6
00:00:17.188 --> 00:00:20.706
Treat every on-demand run as
a change with a second person,

7
00:00:20.706 --> 00:00:23.401
because it can disable
the wrong ten people.

8
00:00:23.401 --> 00:00:26.199
Size execution limits so a reorganization

9
00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:29.075
gets quarantined until
someone approves it.

10
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:33.887
For urgent terminations, don't wait
for the schedule: disable and revoke.

11
00:00:33.887 --> 00:00:37.441
And until PIV revoke and
device retire are automated,

12
00:00:37.441 --> 00:00:39.863
keep a leaver checklist with owners.

13
00:00:39.863 --> 00:00:41.860
Next, what still needs AD.
